{"parentUuid":"7a35eb15-bdde-42d4-bfd3-4183212b6273","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"39a2175a-86b7-4583-b12f-5ec4cbd049f6","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019Ct6oSnMNkC64yHNthnKnb","type":"tool_result","content":"- Export: the \"...\" menu has **Download CSV** and **Download Excel**. Player\n  Traits and Advanced Stats are separate tabs, so separate files. The page shows\n  no ID, but the CSV carries a `PlayerId` column (see the CSV check below), so\n  the two files can be joined on it.\n- Scope picker (top left, default \"Power Four\"): League options **FBS, FCS,\n  Transfer Portal, Group of Six**, every FBS and FCS conference, every team,\n  public lists (All-Americans, Senior Bowl, Combine, pre-season All-Americans)\n  and Baylor's custom lists (for example \"BU ROSTER 26\", \"Baylor Scouting\n  Reports\", \"FALL 26' - PORTAL NEEDS\"). FCS plus Group of Six is a native filter.\n- Season: 2019 to 2026.\n- Filter panel: Positions, States, Classes, Eligibility years left, Minimum Snaps\n  (default 1).\n- Position groups: QB, RB, WR, TE, OT, IOL, IDL, EDGE, OB-LB, SAF, CB.\n- No \"last updated\" date anywhere on the page. Refresh timing still has to be\n  learned by watching or asking Telemetry.\n- Early 2026 caution: most trait cells are \"---\" at two or three games. Top 26\n  Power Four QBs all showed \"---\" for Play Speed, Burst, CoD and both throw\n  velocities. A weekly load will be thin until conference play.\n\n### Columns shown\n\nEvery view: Rank, Player, #, Pos., Class, Elig., Height, Weight, Team,\nHometown, State, Snaps.\n\n| View | Metric columns |\n|---|---|\n| QB Player Traits | Accuracy, Pocket Awareness, Target Selection, INT Avoidance, Adj. Throw Velocity, Max Throw Velocity, Risk Level, Tackle Breaking, Play Speed, Burst, CoD |\n| WR Player Traits | Ball Skills, Tackle Breaking, Elusiveness, Play Speed, Deep Speed, Burst, CoD, Decel, Run Blocking |\n| QB Advanced Stats | Player Impact, Passing Production, Passing Effectiveness, Evasion Rate, Batdowns, Rushing Production, Rushing Effectiveness, Tackles Avoided, Yards After Contact, Top End Speed, Adjusted Speed, Power Speed |\n| WR Advanced Stats | Player Impact, Receiving Production, Receiving Effectiveness, Separation, YAC Over Expected, Tackles Avoided, Yards After Contact, Penalty Drawn, Penalty, Top End Speed, Adjusted Speed, Power Speed |\n\nOther position groups were not opened.\n\n### Mismatches against PORTAL INPUT (67 fixed columns)\n\n- **QB gap is structural.** The QB Player Traits view has no Deep Speed and no\n  Decel column at all. Not a bad export. Answers item 4.\n- **Position codes.** Leaderboard WRs come through as **OWR / SWR**. POSITION\n  MAP only knows WR (its note says \"Telemetry does not split slot\"), so the\n  Baylor tab lookup would go blank for every receiver. Upside: the split can\n  drive WR versus SLOT directly, which `docs/open-work.md` asks for. The\n----\n\nDownloaded with Eric's go-ahead. The file stayed in Downloads under Chrome's\ntemp name (`e5ac3892-...tmp`); nothing was saved to Drive or the repo.\n\nExact header row, in order:\n\n`PlayerId, Rank, Player, #, Pos., Class, Elig., Height, Weight, Team, Hometown,\nState, Snaps, Ball Skills, Tackle Breaking, Elusiveness, Play Speed, Deep Speed,\nBurst, CoD, Decel, Run Blocking`\n\n- **PlayerId exists** (for example `DIX214658`), unique on all 199 rows. That is\n  the join key for Player Traits and Advanced Stats files.\n- **Team is a text slug** (`southern-california`, `michigan-st`, `baylor`), not\n  a display name.\n- Formats: `#` is `#17`, Height is `6-2` text, Elig. is a number, blanks are\n  empty strings (not `---`). File starts with a UTF-8 byte order mark.\n- 199 players: 132 OWR, 67 SWR. Snaps 10 to 163 (Minimum Snaps filter at 1).\n- Header match against PORTAL INPUT row 4: exact matches are Player, Class,\n  Hometown, Snaps, Ball Skills, Tackle Breaking, Play Speed, Deep Speed, Burst,\n  CoD, Decel, Run Blocking. No exact match: PlayerId, Rank, # (none), Pos.\n  (PORTAL: \"Pos (Telemetry)\"), Elig. (\"Elig Yrs\"), Height (\"HT (in)\", inches),\n  Weight (\"WT\"), Team (no equivalent; not Prev Team), State (PORTAL folds it\n  into Hometown), Elusiveness (no column).\n- **Week 3 coverage is nearly empty.** Non-blank values out of 199: Ball Skills\n  8; Play Speed, Deep Speed, Burst, Run Blocking 2 each; Tackle Breaking,\n  Elusiveness, CoD, Decel 0. A weekly load right now would grade almost no WRs.\n  The 30 to 50 per position target depends on data filling in by week 5 or 6,\n  or on loading 2025 season values alongside.\n\n### Still unconfirmed\n\n----\n# 2026-09-30: 2026 FBS test load on a copy of 016 (STATUS Next item 0)\n\n## Result: pass\n\nA scratch copy of 016 was pointed at Drive `_exports/2026_asof_2026-09-29/fbs`\n(UPDATE DATA `LoadFolder`, Min Elig 1) and refreshed through Excel COM\n(`QueryTable.Refresh(False)`: PortalInput, then LoadStatusTable). 016 on Drive\nwas not opened for writing; no new numbered deliverable.\n\nLOAD STATUS:\n\n| Item | 2026 FBS (wk 5) | 2025 as shipped in 016 |\n|---|---|---|\n| CSV files read | 22 | 44 |\n| Players in the files | 9,541 | 19,466 |\n| Players loaded (Elig 1+) | 7,623 | 12,029 |\n| Left out (below Min Elig) | 1,918 | 7,437 |\n| 2025 benchmark players among them | 118 | 132 |\n| Unmapped position codes | ST only | ST only |\n| CSV columns not used | none | none |\n| Capacity check (20,000) | OK | OK |\n| REVIEW flags | 1,077 | 2,121 |\n| REVIEW with Sample OK | 797 | 1,930 |\n\n`manifest_2026_fbs.json` in the folder is ignored (loader reads `.csv` only).\nPositions come from the CSV `Pos.` column, not the file name.\n\nTime on this laptop with ~0.3 GB RAM free: PortalInput 153 s, LoadStatus 64 s,\ntotal 220 s (vs about 2 min for 44 files on 9/29 with memory free). Tell Mauro\nto expect 2-4 minutes.\n\nREVIEW + Sample OK by Baylor tab (the working board; Mauro wants 30-50 per position):\n\n| Tab | Players | REVIEW + Sample OK |\n|---|---|---|\n| QB | 293 | 41 |\n| RB | 600 | 28 |\n| WR, SLOT | 1,071 | 99 |\n| TE | 543 | 32 |\n| OT | 473 | 98 |\n----\n10:  (name LoadFolder), minimum Elig. (LoadMinElig), the LoadStatus table, and\n17:- BENCHMARK PROFILES frozen as values (the appended Elig 0 reference rows go\n133:        wb.Names.Add(\"LoadMinElig\", \"='\" + tmp.Name + \"'!$A$2\")\n194:        ud.Range(\"A12\").Value = \"Minimum Elig. to keep\"\n196:        ud.Range(\"C12\").Value = (\"Telemetry's Elig. is years left after this season. 1 keeps players \"\n199:        wb.Names.Add(\"LoadMinElig\", \"='UPDATE DATA'!$B$12\")\n218:             f'=IF(B{r + 1}>B{r + 2},\"TOO MANY PLAYERS: raise Minimum Elig. or load fewer files\",\"OK\")', \"\"),\n279:                    \"leaderboard (FBS and FCS, Elig 1+). Traits and Advanced Stats rows are merged per \"\n\n- Joins Player Traits and Advanced Stats rows on the CSV's `PlayerId`.\n- Maps header names that differ (`Pos.`, `Elig.`, `Weight`, `Team`, throw\n  velocities, Top End Speed). Converts Height `6-2` to inches. Folds State into\n  Hometown. Team slug goes into Prev Team.\n- Maps leaderboard position codes to POSITION MAP codes (OWR and SWR to WR, and\n  the POSITION MAP aliases). The raw code is kept.\n- `--min-elig 1` keeps players still eligible after the current season. Telemetry's\n  `Elig.` and `Class` are current values even in past-season files (verified\n  2026-09-15), so do not add a year for an older season.\n- PlayerId, raw position, Elusiveness and source file go in columns after Notes.\n  Columns A:BO keep their meaning, so REVIEW BOARD, traits graded and elite share\n  are unchanged.\n- Builds the workbook through **Excel COM**, never openpyxl save (that strips the\n  conditional formatting). Refuses to overwrite an existing file. Extends\n  PORTAL INPUT and REVIEW BOARD rows past the template's last row when needed.\nShell cwd was reset to G:\\My Drive\\00_Primary_Storage_Drive\\02_SPORTS\\Football\\PP_Recruiting","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"dc9c2ef2-baa4-4c46-8758-ef6c4377734d","timestamp":"2026-10-06T19:55:55.083Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"- Export: the \"...\" menu has **Download CSV** and **Download Excel**. Player\n  Traits and Advanced Stats are separate tabs, so separate files. The page shows\n  no ID, but the CSV carries a `PlayerId` column (see the CSV check below), so\n  the two files can be joined on it.\n- Scope picker (top left, default \"Power Four\"): League options **FBS, FCS,\n  Transfer Portal, Group of Six**, every FBS and FCS conference, every team,\n  public lists (All-Americans, Senior Bowl, Combine, pre-season All-Americans)\n  and Baylor's custom lists (for example \"BU ROSTER 26\", \"Baylor Scouting\n  Reports\", \"FALL 26' - PORTAL NEEDS\"). FCS plus Group of Six is a native filter.\n- Season: 2019 to 2026.\n- Filter panel: Positions, States, Classes, Eligibility years left, Minimum Snaps\n  (default 1).\n- Position groups: QB, RB, WR, TE, OT, IOL, IDL, EDGE, OB-LB, SAF, CB.\n- No \"last updated\" date anywhere on the page. Refresh timing still has to be\n  learned by watching or asking Telemetry.\n- Early 2026 caution: most trait cells are \"---\" at two or three games. Top 26\n  Power Four QBs all showed \"---\" for Play Speed, Burst, CoD and both throw\n  velocities. A weekly load will be thin until conference play.\n\n### Columns shown\n\nEvery view: Rank, Player, #, Pos., Class, Elig., Height, Weight, Team,\nHometown, State, Snaps.\n\n| View | Metric columns |\n|---|---|\n| QB Player Traits | Accuracy, Pocket Awareness, Target Selection, INT Avoidance, Adj. Throw Velocity, Max Throw Velocity, Risk Level, Tackle Breaking, Play Speed, Burst, CoD |\n| WR Player Traits | Ball Skills, Tackle Breaking, Elusiveness, Play Speed, Deep Speed, Burst, CoD, Decel, Run Blocking |\n| QB Advanced Stats | Player Impact, Passing Production, Passing Effectiveness, Evasion Rate, Batdowns, Rushing Production, Rushing Effectiveness, Tackles Avoided, Yards After Contact, Top End Speed, Adjusted Speed, Power Speed |\n| WR Advanced Stats | Player Impact, Receiving Production, Receiving Effectiveness, Separation, YAC Over Expected, Tackles Avoided, Yards After Contact, Penalty Drawn, Penalty, Top End Speed, Adjusted Speed, Power Speed |\n\nOther position groups were not opened.\n\n### Mismatches against PORTAL INPUT (67 fixed columns)\n\n- **QB gap is structural.** The QB Player Traits view has no Deep Speed and no\n  Decel column at all. Not a bad export. Answers item 4.\n- **Position codes.** Leaderboard WRs come through as **OWR / SWR**. POSITION\n  MAP only knows WR (its note says \"Telemetry does not split slot\"), so the\n  Baylor tab lookup would go blank for every receiver. Upside: the split can\n  drive WR versus SLOT directly, which `docs/open-work.md` asks for. The\n----\n\nDownloaded with Eric's go-ahead. The file stayed in Downloads under Chrome's\ntemp name (`e5ac3892-...tmp`); nothing was saved to Drive or the repo.\n\nExact header row, in order:\n\n`PlayerId, Rank, Player, #, Pos., Class, Elig., Height, Weight, Team, Hometown,\nState, Snaps, Ball Skills, Tackle Breaking, Elusiveness, Play Speed, Deep Speed,\nBurst, CoD, Decel, Run Blocking`\n\n- **PlayerId exists** (for example `DIX214658`), unique on all 199 rows. That is\n  the join key for Player Traits and Advanced Stats files.\n- **Team is a text slug** (`southern-california`, `michigan-st`, `baylor`), not\n  a display name.\n- Formats: `#` is `#17`, Height is `6-2` text, Elig. is a number, blanks are\n  empty strings (not `---`). File starts with a UTF-8 byte order mark.\n- 199 players: 132 OWR, 67 SWR. Snaps 10 to 163 (Minimum Snaps filter at 1).\n- Header match against PORTAL INPUT row 4: exact matches are Player, Class,\n  Hometown, Snaps, Ball Skills, Tackle Breaking, Play Speed, Deep Speed, Burst,\n  CoD, Decel, Run Blocking. No exact match: PlayerId, Rank, # (none), Pos.\n  (PORTAL: \"Pos (Telemetry)\"), Elig. (\"Elig Yrs\"), Height (\"HT (in)\", inches),\n  Weight (\"WT\"), Team (no equivalent; not Prev Team), State (PORTAL folds it\n  into Hometown), Elusiveness (no column).\n- **Week 3 coverage is nearly empty.** Non-blank values out of 199: Ball Skills\n  8; Play Speed, Deep Speed, Burst, Run Blocking 2 each; Tackle Breaking,\n  Elusiveness, CoD, Decel 0. A weekly load right now would grade almost no WRs.\n  The 30 to 50 per position target depends on data filling in by week 5 or 6,\n  or on loading 2025 season values alongside.\n\n### Still unconfirmed\n\n----\n# 2026-09-30: 2026 FBS test load on a copy of 016 (STATUS Next item 0)\n\n## Result: pass\n\nA scratch copy of 016 was pointed at Drive `_exports/2026_asof_2026-09-29/fbs`\n(UPDATE DATA `LoadFolder`, Min Elig 1) and refreshed through Excel COM\n(`QueryTable.Refresh(False)`: PortalInput, then LoadStatusTable). 016 on Drive\nwas not opened for writing; no new numbered deliverable.\n\nLOAD STATUS:\n\n| Item | 2026 FBS (wk 5) | 2025 as shipped in 016 |\n|---|---|---|\n| CSV files read | 22 | 44 |\n| Players in the files | 9,541 | 19,466 |\n| Players loaded (Elig 1+) | 7,623 | 12,029 |\n| Left out (below Min Elig) | 1,918 | 7,437 |\n| 2025 benchmark players among them | 118 | 132 |\n| Unmapped position codes | ST only | ST only |\n| CSV columns not used | none | none |\n| Capacity check (20,000) | OK | OK |\n| REVIEW flags | 1,077 | 2,121 |\n| REVIEW with Sample OK | 797 | 1,930 |\n\n`manifest_2026_fbs.json` in the folder is ignored (loader reads `.csv` only).\nPositions come from the CSV `Pos.` column, not the file name.\n\nTime on this laptop with ~0.3 GB RAM free: PortalInput 153 s, LoadStatus 64 s,\ntotal 220 s (vs about 2 min for 44 files on 9/29 with memory free). Tell Mauro\nto expect 2-4 minutes.\n\nREVIEW + Sample OK by Baylor tab (the working board; Mauro wants 30-50 per position):\n\n| Tab | Players | REVIEW + Sample OK |\n|---|---|---|\n| QB | 293 | 41 |\n| RB | 600 | 28 |\n| WR, SLOT | 1,071 | 99 |\n| TE | 543 | 32 |\n| OT | 473 | 98 |\n----\n10:  (name LoadFolder), minimum Elig. (LoadMinElig), the LoadStatus table, and\n17:- BENCHMARK PROFILES frozen as values (the appended Elig 0 reference rows go\n133:        wb.Names.Add(\"LoadMinElig\", \"='\" + tmp.Name + \"'!$A$2\")\n194:        ud.Range(\"A12\").Value = \"Minimum Elig. to keep\"\n196:        ud.Range(\"C12\").Value = (\"Telemetry's Elig. is years left after this season. 1 keeps players \"\n199:        wb.Names.Add(\"LoadMinElig\", \"='UPDATE DATA'!$B$12\")\n218:             f'=IF(B{r + 1}>B{r + 2},\"TOO MANY PLAYERS: raise Minimum Elig. or load fewer files\",\"OK\")', \"\"),\n279:                    \"leaderboard (FBS and FCS, Elig 1+). Traits and Advanced Stats rows are merged per \"\n\n- Joins Player Traits and Advanced Stats rows on the CSV's `PlayerId`.\n- Maps header names that differ (`Pos.`, `Elig.`, `Weight`, `Team`, throw\n  velocities, Top End Speed). Converts Height `6-2` to inches. Folds State into\n  Hometown. Team slug goes into Prev Team.\n- Maps leaderboard position codes to POSITION MAP codes (OWR and SWR to WR, and\n  the POSITION MAP aliases). The raw code is kept.\n- `--min-elig 1` keeps players still eligible after the current season. Telemetry's\n  `Elig.` and `Class` are current values even in past-season files (verified\n  2026-09-15), so do not add a year for an older season.\n- PlayerId, raw position, Elusiveness and source file go in columns after Notes.\n  Columns A:BO keep their meaning, so REVIEW BOARD, traits graded and elite share\n  are unchanged.\n- Builds the workbook through **Excel COM**, never openpyxl save (that strips the\n  conditional formatting). Refuses to overwrite an existing file. Extends\n  PORTAL INPUT and REVIEW BOARD rows past the template's last row when needed.","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to G:\\My Drive\\00_Primary_Storage_Drive\\02_SPORTS\\Football\\PP_Recruiting","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"7a35eb15-bdde-42d4-bfd3-4183212b6273","session_id":"