{"parentUuid":"26fbca3e-0560-49fe-a006-b5f69225492f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfmbH3r75QqdXC9zjA3YG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Confirmed: neither file in `10.6.26 TELEMETRY DUMP` has an `Elig.` column. These two files also aren't in the format the 9/29 pull produced, and eligibility isn't the only thing that's different.\n\n| | 9/29 pull (`_exports/2026_asof_2026-09-29`) | 10/6 dump |\n|---|---|---|\n| `Elig.` column | yes, column 7 | **missing** |\n| Height | `6-4` | **`Jun-00`** (Excel turned `6-0` into a date) |\n| Team | slug (`southern-california`) | short code (`OHYO`) |\n| Quoting | every field quoted | none |\n| QB rows | 264 traits / 372 adv (FBS only) | 416 / 711 (looks like FBS + FCS) |\n\nThe 10/6 files have two more problems:\n\n1. **The file names are swapped.** `QB ADV (26).csv` holds the trait columns (Accuracy, Pocket Awareness…). `QB TRAITS (26).csv` holds the advanced stats (Player Impact, Passing Production…). The loader goes by column headers, so this won't break the load, but anyone reading the files will be misled.\n2. **The heights are wrong.** At least some cells were saved as dates (`Jun-00`, which was `6-0`), which means the files were opened and saved in Excel at some point. The loader can't turn `Jun-00` back into inches. Any affected player would get a blank or wrong HT, which feeds the Size factor.\n\n**Why `Elig.` is missing:** the files can't tell me for sure. Saving in Excel explains the dates and the lost quotes, but it doesn't delete a column. The team codes instead of slugs, the extra FCS rows and the missing `Elig.` suggest a different export path. My best guesses:\n- **Download Excel** instead of **Download CSV**\n- the **Transfer Portal** grid instead of **Leaderboards**\n- a leaderboard view with the Elig. column hidden\n\nThe 9/15 meeting notes list Elig. as a column on every Leaderboard view, and both the manual load and the Power Query load in 014 and later expect it.\n\n**To fix it:** export again from **Leaderboards → Player Traits / Advanced Stats → More options → Download CSV**, and load the file **without opening it in Excel first**. `scripts/telemetry_pull.py` does this for all 22 groups and is what produced the 9/29 set. You could also check whether the Elig. column appears on screen in the view you exported from. If it's there on screen but missing from the file, Telemetry has changed its export, and we'd need another source for eligibility, such as joining on PlayerId to the 9/29 files.\n\nI haven't changed anything in the dump folder. Should I re-pull the QBs (or all groups) with `telemetry_pull.py`? It needs your Chrome session logged in to Telemetry."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":893,"cache_read_input_tokens":105822,"output_tokens":1343,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":378},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":893,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1343,"cache_read_input_tokens":105822,"cache_creation_input_tokens":893,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":893},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfmbH3Zixvzv9hHpjwEbc","type":"assistant","uuid":"3ffabbb9-ac07-4243-8f4b-bd80eed9b91f","timestamp":"2026-10-06T20:11:17.495Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"d1673601-88f7-4fb0-b59a-00f5414c1656","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"G:\\My Drive\\00_Primary_Storage_Drive\\02_SPORTS\\Football\\PP_Recruiting","sessionId":"d1673601-88f7-4fb0-b59a-00f5414c1656"