{"parentUuid":"049d612c-82b7-44ef-b5ef-4907084c9ac8","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6f298c9c-1529-4ddf-9e74-0070d06bed9d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017ZEVpaATh1oKYBsrQTAUDM","type":"tool_result","content":"HONORS BENCHMARK tab differs.\n\n## 2026-09-30 Codex check of 017; 018 ships (provenance fix, no number changes)\n\n**Codex check of 017:** Wester fix, all 1,104 median/n comparisons, the 40-cell\ndiff versus 016 and the Send copy (byte-identical) passed. One provenance finding:\nCooper DeJean's 2023 SI All-America row (raw row 627, \"All-purpose / return\nspecialist\") is a kick-returner award and still counted, so the A3 note overstated\nthe return exclusion. No numerical effect: his DB All-America (raw row 606) keeps\nhim in. Report: repo `docs/audits/2026-09-30-codex-check-017.md`.\n\n**Fix:** `RETURN_ROLE` in `honors_match.py` is now keyed to one raw row (season,\nsource, player, heading, selectors), so an exception cannot drop a player's other\nhonors from the same source; DeJean's SI row added; the matcher stops if any entry\nfails to match exactly one row. A3 note rewritten: a combined honor counts only\nwhen the selector named the player all-purpose (return selections checked and\nexcluded) and he holds a position honor that season. v4 outputs in\n`_exports/honors/superseded_2026-09-30_v4/`. Result: benchmark CSV identical; only\nDeJean's Honors text in `2023_matched.csv` changed.\n\n**018 shipped:** `018. BAYLOR - TELEMETRY x STAQS UNIFIED GRADING (HONORS\nBENCHMARK).xlsx`, built from 014. Versus 017: 1 cell (HONORS BENCHMARK A3), same\n12 sheets, 0 error cells; `check_workbook.py` ALL CHECKS PASS. In `Send/`. 017\nalso stays in `Send/` because Eric is sending it to Mauro today (every number in\n017 and 018 is the same). Next number is 019.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"dfa5caa8-0627-431c-a6d8-5e378337075b","timestamp":"2026-10-06T20:22:37.807Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"HONORS BENCHMARK tab differs.\n\n## 2026-09-30 Codex check of 017; 018 ships (provenance fix, no number changes)\n\n**Codex check of 017:** Wester fix, all 1,104 median/n comparisons, the 40-cell\ndiff versus 016 and the Send copy (byte-identical) passed. One provenance finding:\nCooper DeJean's 2023 SI All-America row (raw row 627, \"All-purpose / return\nspecialist\") is a kick-returner award and still counted, so the A3 note overstated\nthe return exclusion. No numerical effect: his DB All-America (raw row 606) keeps\nhim in. Report: repo `docs/audits/2026-09-30-codex-check-017.md`.\n\n**Fix:** `RETURN_ROLE` in `honors_match.py` is now keyed to one raw row (season,\nsource, player, heading, selectors), so an exception cannot drop a player's other\nhonors from the same source; DeJean's SI row added; the matcher stops if any entry\nfails to match exactly one row. A3 note rewritten: a combined honor counts only\nwhen the selector named the player all-purpose (return selections checked and\nexcluded) and he holds a position honor that season. v4 outputs in\n`_exports/honors/superseded_2026-09-30_v4/`. Result: benchmark CSV identical; only\nDeJean's Honors text in `2023_matched.csv` changed.\n\n**018 shipped:** `018. BAYLOR - TELEMETRY x STAQS UNIFIED GRADING (HONORS\nBENCHMARK).xlsx`, built from 014. Versus 017: 1 cell (HONORS BENCHMARK A3), same\n12 sheets, 0 error cells; `check_workbook.py` ALL CHECKS PASS. In `Send/`. 017\nalso stays in `Send/` because Eric is sending it to Mauro today (every number in\n017 and 018 is the same). Next number is 019.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"049d612c-82b7-44ef-b5ef-4907084c9ac8","session_id":"d1673601-88f7-4fb0-b59a-00f5414c1656","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"G:\\My Drive\\00_Primary_Storage_Drive\\02_SPORTS\\Football\\PP_Recruiting","sessionId":"d1673601-88f7-4fb0-b59a-00f5414c1656","version":"2.1.291","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
