{"parentUuid":"2f974dde-67b8-4464-9a9a-162e9f80696c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfmcsPkEayceAnTWc5XcC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018PEioxPxEW9GSbMCQyPnhj","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd \"/c/Users/eric_rash/Desktop/DEV/PP_Recruiting\"; sed -n 1,80p scripts/telemetry_pull.py; echo; wc -l scripts/telemetry_pull.py; echo ----; cat docs/handoffs/2026-09-29-2026-fbs-pull.md; echo ----; sed -n 310,360p docs/STATUS.md","description":"Read the pull script header and pull notes"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":183,"cache_read_input_tokens":110001,"output_tokens":296,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":49},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":183,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":296,"cache_read_input_tokens":110001,"cache_creation_input_tokens":183,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":183},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_018PEioxPxEW9GSbMCQyPnhj":{"command":"cd \"/c/Users/eric_rash/Desktop/DEV/PP_Recruiting\"; sed -n 1,80p scripts/telemetry_pull.py; echo; wc -l scripts/telemetry_pull.py; echo ----; cat docs/handoffs/2026-09-29-2026-fbs-pull.md; echo ----; sed -n 310,360p docs/STATUS.md","description":"Read the pull script header and pull notes"}},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CfmcsPMAq9PAtvpQ7HteK","type":"assistant","uuid":"b2e12fe0-248b-4a1b-96ab-4db5d455d067","timestamp":"2026-10-06T20:31:59.598Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"d1673601-88f7-4fb0-b59a-00f5414c1656","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"G:\\My Drive\\00_Primary_Storage_Drive\\02_SPORTS\\Football\\PP_Recruiting","sessionId":"d1673601-88f7-4fb0-b59a-00f5414c1656","version":"2.1.291","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
{"parentUuid":"b2e12fe0-248b-4a1b-96ab-4db5d455d067","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_non_blocking_error","hookName":"PreToolUse:Bash","toolUseID":"toolu_018PEioxPxEW9GSbMCQyPnhj","hookEvent":"PreToolUse","stderr":"Failed with non-blocking status code: /usr/bin/bash: line 1: /Users/kristinarash/.local/bin/dcg: No such file or directory","stdout":"","exitCode":127,"command":"/Users/kristinarash/.local/bin/dcg","durationMs":141},"type":"attachment","uuid":"5b31de53-fdce-4cfc-a8fb-eb73853fb50d","timestamp":"2026-10-06T20:31:59.779Z","session_id":"d1673601-88f7-4fb0-b59a-00f5414c1656","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"G:\\My Drive\\00_Primary_Storage_Drive\\02_SPORTS\\Football\\PP_Recruiting","sessionId":"d1673601-88f7-4fb0-b59a-00f5414c1656","version":"2.1.291","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
{"parentUuid":"b2e12fe0-248b-4a1b-96ab-4db5d455d067","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"4b841993-72e3-4854-a61a-b7073d9f14da","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018PEioxPxEW9GSbMCQyPnhj","type":"tool_result","content":"\"\"\"telemetry-pull: download Telemetry leaderboard CSVs (Player Traits and Advanced\nStats, every position group) for one season and scope, into a named folder.\n\nDrives the installed Chrome with Playwright through the same clicks a person\nmakes (scope, season, group, More options > Download CSV). The CSV the page\nbuilds for that click is kept byte for byte from the page itself rather than\nthrough Chrome's download manager, which crashed Chrome on this machine a few\nseconds after each download (2026-09-29). Read-only: it never\nedits anything in Telemetry, never reads the auth token and never calls the\ninternal API (project rule, Drive AGENTS.md section 2). It uses its own Chrome\nprofile, so log in once with --login; Eric types the password himself.\n\nEach file is checked as it lands (tab by header, position group by Pos. codes,\nrows > 0, not a repeat of the previous file) and written as\n<season>_<scope>_<GROUP>_<player-traits|advanced-stats>.csv, the naming in\n_exports/. A manifest.json records row counts, team counts and top snaps.\nExisting files are never overwritten.\n\nUsage (from the repo root):\n  uv run --with playwright python scripts/telemetry_pull.py --login     (once; log in, it closes itself)\n  uv run --with playwright python scripts/telemetry_pull.py --season 2026 --scope FBS ^\n      --out \"G:/My Drive/00_Primary_Storage_Drive/02_SPORTS/Football/PP_Recruiting/_exports/2026_wk05/fbs\"\n  ... --scope \"FCS,Group of Six\" --tag fcs-g6 --out \".../fcs_g6\"   (several scopes; 2025 folder layout)\n  ... --groups QB RB --tabs traits                        (subset, for testing)\n  ... --probe                                             (print the page's controls; no downloads)\n\nKeep the Chrome window it opens visible until it finishes (Telemetry stalls\ndownloads in a hidden window).\n\"\"\"\n\nimport argparse\nimport base64\nimport csv\nimport io\nimport json\nimport os\nimport re\nimport sys\nimport time\nfrom collections import Counter\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nURL = \"https://app.telemetry.fm/ncaa/leaderboard/{tab}\"\nTABS = {\"traits\": (\"player-traits\", \"Player Traits\"), \"advanced\": (\"advanced-stats\", \"Advanced Stats\")}\n# Group as named in the leaderboard dropdown -> file tag, and the Pos. codes it holds.\nGROUPS = {\n    \"QB\": (\"QB\", {\"QB\"}),\n    \"RB\": (\"RB\", {\"HB\", \"FB\", \"RB\"}),\n    \"WR\": (\"WR\", {\"OWR\", \"SWR\", \"WR\"}),\n    \"TE\": (\"TE\", {\"H\", \"Y\", \"F\", \"TE\"}),\n    \"OT\": (\"OT\", {\"LT\", \"RT\", \"OT\", \"T\"}),\n    \"IOL\": (\"IOL\", {\"LG\", \"RG\", \"C\", \"OG\", \"G\"}),\n    \"IDL\": (\"IDL\", {\"DT\", \"NT\", \"DL\"}),\n    \"EDGE\": (\"EDGE\", {\"UP\", \"DOWN\", \"DE\", \"EDGE\"}),\n    \"OB-LB\": (\"OB-LB\", {\"ILB\", \"OLB\", \"LB\", \"UP\"}),\n    \"CB\": (\"CB\", {\"OCB\", \"SCB\", \"CB\"}),\n    \"SAF\": (\"SAF\", {\"FS\", \"SS\", \"SAF\", \"SCB\"}),\n}\nDEFAULT_PROFILE = Path(os.environ.get(\"LOCALAPPDATA\", Path.home())) / \"telemetry-pull\" / \"chrome-profile\"\n\n# Tags the page's controls so Playwright can address them by role, not by position.\nTAG_JS = r\"\"\"\n() => {\n  const inputs = [...document.querySelectorAll('input')].filter(i => i.offsetParent !== null);\n  const out = {};\n  for (const i of inputs) {\n    const v = (i.value || '').trim();\n    if (/^(19|20)\\d\\d$/.test(v)) { i.setAttribute('data-tp', 'season'); out.season = v; }\n    else if (/(Player Traits|Advanced Stats)$/.test(v)) { i.setAttribute('data-tp', 'group'); out.group = v; }\n    else if ((i.placeholder || '').toLowerCase() === 'search') { i.setAttribute('data-tp', 'search'); }\n  }\n  // Scope: the multiselect whose wrapper holds the chips (first pill input on the filter row).\n  // Only the chip labels: the wrapper divs also match \"Pill\" and repeat every chip's text.\n  const pills = [...document.querySelectorAll('[class*=\"Pill-label\"]')].filter(p => p.offsetParent !== null);\n  out.scopes = pills.map(p => p.textContent.trim()).filter(Boolean);\n  const pillInput = document.querySelector('[class*=\"PillsInput\"] input, [class*=\"pillsInput\"] input');\n  if (pillInput) { pillInput.setAttribute('data-tp', 'scope'); }\n  const more = [...document.querySelectorAll('button')].filter(b => b.offsetParent !== null &&\n      /more options/i.test((b.getAttribute('aria-label') || '') + ' ' + (b.title || '')));\n  if (more.length) { more[more.length - 1].setAttribute('data-tp', 'more'); out.more = true; }\n\n386 scripts/telemetry_pull.py\n----\n# 2026-09-29: 2026 FBS leaderboard pull done, telemetry_pull.py download fix\n\n## What and why\n\nEric wanted the 2026 Telemetry leaderboard exports pulled automatically (Playwright CLI,\n`scripts/telemetry_pull.py`) so the 2026 test load and the Mauro walkthrough can go ahead.\nA parallel session (`docs/handoffs/2026-09-29-telemetry-pull-fix.md`) fixed the scope\nfilter; the full run then kept dying at the first or second download.\n\n## Findings and decisions\n\n- Two sessions were driving the same tool profile. Only one run at a time works.\n- The real failure was Chrome crashing a few seconds after each download completes\n  (Crashpad dumps in `%LOCALAPPDATA%\\telemetry-pull\\chrome-profile\\Crashpad\\reports`,\n  5:25 to 5:44 PM, naming `Downloads\\desktop.ini` / LEGACY_DOWNLOAD). Small files won\n  the race with `save_as`; RB always lost. Setting `downloads_path` alone did not help.\n- Fix (`93e8829`): before clicking Download CSV, the tool hooks `URL.createObjectURL`\n  on the page, keeps the export blob, holds back the anchor click, and writes the raw\n  bytes (base64 from `arrayBuffer`, so the UTF-8 BOM survives). Verified byte-identical\n  to a Chrome-saved file (QB traits). Still UI-only: no token, no internal API.\n- Manifest now merges across reruns (skipped files keep their entries).\n\n## Files\n\n- `scripts/telemetry_pull.py` (commit `93e8829`)\n- `docs/STATUS.md`, this handoff\n- Drive `_exports/2026_asof_2026-09-29/fbs/`: 22 CSVs (`2026_fbs_<GROUP>_<player-traits|advanced-stats>.csv`)\n  and `manifest_2026_fbs.json` (22 entries; QB traits entry added by hand from the file)\n\nChecks: 138 teams per file (RB traits 137), headers and BOM identical to the matching\n2025 FBS file, all 22 files distinct.\n\n## Next\n\n1. 2026 test load into a copy of 015 (UPDATE DATA, Refresh All, LOAD STATUS).\n2. FCS pull: decide FCS only vs FCS + G6 (2025 used `fcs_g6`).\n3. Mauro walkthrough; confirm Windows Excel.\n4. Codex re-check of 015 (F2-F9) still outstanding.\n5. Document telemetry_pull.py in `scripts/README.md`.\n----\n- **Validation P4 files are subsets.** In `_exports/2025_baseline/\n  validation_fbs_fcs/`, only the two QB files are full; the 16\n  `*_recap-subset.csv` hold only recap players. Fine for grading those players\n  (percentiles do not change with scope), useless for sizing alerts.\n- **Downloads from automation (2026-09-16):** with the Chrome window hidden or\n  minimized (`document.hidden` true), screenshots and timers stall and\n  scripted downloads stop after the first one, even with \"allow multiple\n  downloads\" on. Download CSV is an `<a download>` blob link inside a Radix\n  menu (open it with a pointerdown on \"More options\"; the blob is built when\n  the menu opens, so reopen after the table loads). Workaround used: `fetch()`\n  the blob in the page and read it back, about 1 KB per JavaScript return. For\n  full exports, keep the window visible and click by hand or with real clicks.\n  Mantine selects (scope, season, group) respond to mousedown + click on\n  `[role=option]`. Leaderboard `Top End\n  Speed` looks like a percentile, not mph.\n- **Verify the season before trusting a leaderboard pull.** The season box can\n  read 2025 while the table still shows 2026 (seen 2026-09-16 with the window\n  hidden). Check one known player's snaps against a saved file first\n  (for example Colandrea, UNLV, 794 snaps in 2025).\n- Leaderboard position codes are alignments: OWR/SWR, H/F/Y, LT/RT, LG/C/RG,\n  DT/NT, UP/DOWN, ILB/OLB, FS/SS, OCB/SCB, ST. Both scripts map them; ST shows\n  Baylor tab \"?\".\n- 4,047 of 8,761 rows in 008 are NO DATA: Advanced-Stats-only players carry\n  Player Impact but no traits. FCS has no Ball Skills values. 66 players sit in\n  two position groups and keep the first file's position.\n- **Full FBS pull (2026-09-16) worked** with the window visible: real clicks on\n  \"More options\" > \"Download CSV\", 22 files in a row. The Telemetry app is\n  `https://app.telemetry.fm` (leaderboards at `/ncaa/leaderboard/player-traits`\n  and `/advanced-stats`). The extension may open its own new window, which\n  reports hidden until Eric brings it to the front. Window width can change\n  mid-session and move the toolbar; re-measure click positions. A\n  `browser_batch` of 7 groups timed out (downloads still finished); use 4 or 5.\n  Season can be verified afterwards from file contents (136 teams, top snaps\n  near 800 to 1,000 for a full 2025 FBS file).\n- **G6 players are in both `fcs_g6/` and `fbs/`** (4,968 ids, identical values),\n  so stage both folders together; the loader merges on PlayerId.\n- Telemetry in the browser: Chrome's \"Ask where to save each file\" dialog\n  freezes automation (Eric turned it off 2026-09-15). Switching Player Traits /\n  Advanced Stats tabs resets season, scope and group. Scope \"Clear selection\"\n  does not remove Power Four; untick the option. Click coordinates use the\n  screenshot frame, not page pixels. The Advanced Stats group list adds K and P\n  at the bottom. Check the table has rows before Download CSV (one TE export\n  came back empty).\n- Portal scrape: calendar arrows move two months; \"Apply Filters\" may need a\n  second click; reload if Next is disabled on page 1; the table is virtualized\n  (~20 rows in the DOM).\nShell cwd was reset to G:\\My Drive\\00_Primary_Storage_Drive\\02_SPORTS\\Football\\PP_Recruiting","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"6fcd123a-92b7-4fac-8063-ab134c17e2ee","timestamp":"2026-10-06T20:32:01.506Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"\"\"\"telemetry-pull: download Telemetry leaderboard CSVs (Player Traits and Advanced\nStats, every position group) for one season and scope, into a named folder.\n\nDrives the installed Chrome with Playwright through the same clicks a person\nmakes (scope, season, group, More options > Download CSV). The CSV the page\nbuilds for that click is kept byte for byte from the page itself rather than\nthrough Chrome's download manager, which crashed Chrome on this machine a few\nseconds after each download (2026-09-29). Read-only: it never\nedits anything in Telemetry, never reads the auth token and never calls the\ninternal API (project rule, Drive AGENTS.md section 2). It uses its own Chrome\nprofile, so log in once with --login; Eric types the password himself.\n\nEach file is checked as it lands (tab by header, position group by Pos. codes,\nrows > 0, not a repeat of the previous file) and written as\n<season>_<scope>_<GROUP>_<player-traits|advanced-stats>.csv, the naming in\n_exports/. A manifest.json records row counts, team counts and top snaps.\nExisting files are never overwritten.\n\nUsage (from the repo root):\n  uv run --with playwright python scripts/telemetry_pull.py --login     (once; log in, it closes itself)\n  uv run --with playwright python scripts/telemetry_pull.py --season 2026 --scope FBS ^\n      --out \"G:/My Drive/00_Primary_Storage_Drive/02_SPORTS/Football/PP_Recruiting/_exports/2026_wk05/fbs\"\n  ... --scope \"FCS,Group of Six\" --tag fcs-g6 --out \".../fcs_g6\"   (several scopes; 2025 folder layout)\n  ... --groups QB RB --tabs traits                        (subset, for testing)\n  ... --probe                                             (print the page's controls; no downloads)\n\nKeep the Chrome window it opens visible until it finishes (Telemetry stalls\ndownloads in a hidden window).\n\"\"\"\n\nimport argparse\nimport base64\nimport csv\nimport io\nimport json\nimport os\nimport re\nimport sys\nimport time\nfrom collections import Counter\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nURL = \"https://app.telemetry.fm/ncaa/leaderboard/{tab}\"\nTABS = {\"traits\": (\"player-traits\", \"Player Traits\"), \"advanced\": (\"advanced-stats\", \"Advanced Stats\")}\n# Group as named in the leaderboard dropdown -> file tag, and the Pos. codes it holds.\nGROUPS = {\n    \"QB\": (\"QB\", {\"QB\"}),\n    \"RB\": (\"RB\", {\"HB\", \"FB\", \"RB\"}),\n    \"WR\": (\"WR\", {\"OWR\", \"SWR\", \"WR\"}),\n    \"TE\": (\"TE\", {\"H\", \"Y\", \"F\", \"TE\"}),\n    \"OT\": (\"OT\", {\"LT\", \"RT\", \"OT\", \"T\"}),\n    \"IOL\": (\"IOL\", {\"LG\", \"RG\", \"C\", \"OG\", \"G\"}),\n    \"IDL\": (\"IDL\", {\"DT\", \"NT\", \"DL\"}),\n    \"EDGE\": (\"EDGE\", {\"UP\", \"DOWN\", \"DE\", \"EDGE\"}),\n    \"OB-LB\": (\"OB-LB\", {\"ILB\", \"OLB\", \"LB\", \"UP\"}),\n    \"CB\": (\"CB\", {\"OCB\", \"SCB\", \"CB\"}),\n    \"SAF\": (\"SAF\", {\"FS\", \"SS\", \"SAF\", \"SCB\"}),\n}\nDEFAULT_PROFILE = Path(os.environ.get(\"LOCALAPPDATA\", Path.home())) / \"telemetry-pull\" / \"chrome-profile\"\n\n# Tags the page's controls so Playwright can address them by role, not by position.\nTAG_JS = r\"\"\"\n() => {\n  const inputs = [...document.querySelectorAll('input')].filter(i => i.offsetParent !== null);\n  const out = {};\n  for (const i of inputs) {\n    const v = (i.value || '').trim();\n    if (/^(19|20)\\d\\d$/.test(v)) { i.setAttribute('data-tp', 'season'); out.season = v; }\n    else if (/(Player Traits|Advanced Stats)$/.test(v)) { i.setAttribute('data-tp', 'group'); out.group = v; }\n    else if ((i.placeholder || '').toLowerCase() === 'search') { i.setAttribute('data-tp', 'search'); }\n  }\n  // Scope: the multiselect whose wrapper holds the chips (first pill input on the filter row).\n  // Only the chip labels: the wrapper divs also match \"Pill\" and repeat every chip's text.\n  const pills = [...document.querySelectorAll('[class*=\"Pill-label\"]')].filter(p => p.offsetParent !== null);\n  out.scopes = pills.map(p => p.textContent.trim()).filter(Boolean);\n  const pillInput = document.querySelector('[class*=\"PillsInput\"] input, [class*=\"pillsInput\"] input');\n  if (pillInput) { pillInput.setAttribute('data-tp', 'scope'); }\n  const more = [...document.querySelectorAll('button')].filter(b => b.offsetParent !== null &&\n      /more options/i.test((b.getAttribute('aria-label') || '') + ' ' + (b.title || '')));\n  if (more.length) { more[more.length - 1].setAttribute('data-tp', 'more'); out.more = true; }\n\n386 scripts/telemetry_pull.py\n----\n# 2026-09-29: 2026 FBS leaderboard pull done, telemetry_pull.py download fix\n\n## What and why\n\nEric wanted the 2026 Telemetry leaderboard exports pulled automatically (Playwright CLI,\n`scripts/telemetry_pull.py`) so the 2026 test load and the Mauro walkthrough can go ahead.\nA parallel session (`docs/handoffs/2026-09-29-telemetry-pull-fix.md`) fixed the scope\nfilter; the full run then kept dying at the first or second download.\n\n## Findings and decisions\n\n- Two sessions were driving the same tool profile. Only one run at a time works.\n- The real failure was Chrome crashing a few seconds after each download completes\n  (Crashpad dumps in `%LOCALAPPDATA%\\telemetry-pull\\chrome-profile\\Crashpad\\reports`,\n  5:25 to 5:44 PM, naming `Downloads\\desktop.ini` / LEGACY_DOWNLOAD). Small files won\n  the race with `save_as`; RB always lost. Setting `downloads_path` alone did not help.\n- Fix (`93e8829`): before clicking Download CSV, the tool hooks `URL.createObjectURL`\n  on the page, keeps the export blob, holds back the anchor click, and writes the raw\n  bytes (base64 from `arrayBuffer`, so the UTF-8 BOM survives). Verified byte-identical\n  to a Chrome-saved file (QB traits). Still UI-only: no token, no internal API.\n- Manifest now merges across reruns (skipped files keep their entries).\n\n## Files\n\n- `scripts/telemetry_pull.py` (commit `93e8829`)\n- `docs/STATUS.md`, this handoff\n- Drive `_exports/2026_asof_2026-09-29/fbs/`: 22 CSVs (`2026_fbs_<GROUP>_<player-traits|advanced-stats>.csv`)\n  and `manifest_2026_fbs.json` (22 entries; QB traits entry added by hand from the file)\n\nChecks: 138 teams per file (RB traits 137), headers and BOM identical to the matching\n2025 FBS file, all 22 files distinct.\n\n## Next\n\n1. 2026 test load into a copy of 015 (UPDATE DATA, Refresh All, LOAD STATUS).\n2. FCS pull: decide FCS only vs FCS + G6 (2025 used `fcs_g6`).\n3. Mauro walkthrough; confirm Windows Excel.\n4. Codex re-check of 015 (F2-F9) still outstanding.\n5. Document telemetry_pull.py in `scripts/README.md`.\n----\n- **Validation P4 files are subsets.** In `_exports/2025_baseline/\n  validation_fbs_fcs/`, only the two QB files are full; the 16\n  `*_recap-subset.csv` hold only recap players. Fine for grading those players\n  (percentiles do not change with scope), useless for sizing alerts.\n- **Downloads from automation (2026-09-16):** with the Chrome window hidden or\n  minimized (`document.hidden` true), screenshots and timers stall and\n  scripted downloads stop after the first one, even with \"allow multiple\n  downloads\" on. Download CSV is an `<a download>` blob link inside a Radix\n  menu (open it with a pointerdown on \"More options\"; the blob is built when\n  the menu opens, so reopen after the table loads). Workaround used: `fetch()`\n  the blob in the page and read it back, about 1 KB per JavaScript return. For\n  full exports, keep the window visible and click by hand or with real clicks.\n  Mantine selects (scope, season, group) respond to mousedown + click on\n  `[role=option]`. Leaderboard `Top End\n  Speed` looks like a percentile, not mph.\n- **Verify the season before trusting a leaderboard pull.** The season box can\n  read 2025 while the table still shows 2026 (seen 2026-09-16 with the window\n  hidden). Check one known player's snaps against a saved file first\n  (for example Colandrea, UNLV, 794 snaps in 2025).\n- Leaderboard position codes are alignments: OWR/SWR, H/F/Y, LT/RT, LG/C/RG,\n  DT/NT, UP/DOWN, ILB/OLB, FS/SS, OCB/SCB, ST. Both scripts map them; ST shows\n  Baylor tab \"?\".\n- 4,047 of 8,761 rows in 008 are NO DATA: Advanced-Stats-only players carry\n  Player Impact but no traits. FCS has no Ball Skills values. 66 players sit in\n  two position groups and keep the first file's position.\n- **Full FBS pull (2026-09-16) worked** with the window visible: real clicks on\n  \"More options\" > \"Download CSV\", 22 files in a row. The Telemetry app is\n  `https://app.telemetry.fm` (leaderboards at `/ncaa/leaderboard/player-traits`\n  and `/advanced-stats`). The extension may open its own new window, which\n  reports hidden until Eric brings it to the front. Window width can change\n  mid-session and move the toolbar; re-measure click positions. A\n  `browser_batch` of 7 groups timed out (downloads still finished); use 4 or 5.\n  Season can be verified afterwards from file contents (136 teams, top snaps\n  near 800 to 1,000 for a full 2025 FBS file).\n- **G6 players are in both `fcs_g6/` and `fbs/`** (4,968 ids, identical values),\n  so stage both folders together; the loader merges on PlayerId.\n- Telemetry in the browser: Chrome's \"Ask where to save each file\" dialog\n  freezes automation (Eric turned it off 2026-09-15). Switching Player Traits /\n  Advanced Stats tabs resets season, scope and group. Scope \"Clear selection\"\n  does not remove Power Four; untick the option. Click coordinates use the\n  screenshot frame, not page pixels. The Advanced Stats group list adds K and P\n  at the bottom. Check the table has rows before Download CSV (one TE export\n  came back empty).\n- Portal scrape: calendar arrows move two months; \"Apply Filters\" may need a\n  second click; reload if Next is disabled on page 1; the table is virtualized\n  (~20 rows in the DOM).","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to G:\\My Drive\\00_Primary_Storage_Drive\\02_SPORTS\\Football\\PP_Recruiting","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"b2e12fe0-248b-4a1b-96ab-4db5d455d067","session_id":"d1673601-88f7-4fb0-b59a-00f5414c1656","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"G:\\My Drive\\00_Primary_Storage_Drive\\02_SPORTS\\Football\\PP_Recruiting","sessionId":"d1673601-88f7-4fb0-b59a-00f5414c1656","version":"2.1.291","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
