{"parentUuid":"9b823364-513d-4c31-a81d-c771679629db","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfmctBfEwpLVeSg1rHQPq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1242,"cache_read_input_tokens":114597,"output_tokens":1441,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":493},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1242,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1441,"cache_read_input_tokens":114597,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1242,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1242},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":12496,"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfmctBQMXWmU5MEtVKuoa","type":"assistant","uuid":"ea6590cb-b512-4606-a3ae-0f2a03f6ff27","timestamp":"2026-10-06T20:32:20.180Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"d1673601-88f7-4fb0-b59a-00f5414c1656","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"G:\\My Drive\\00_Primary_Storage_Drive\\02_SPORTS\\Football\\PP_Recruiting","sessionId":"d1673601-88f7-4fb0-b59a-00f5414c1656","version":"2.1.291","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
{"parentUuid":"ea6590cb-b512-4606-a3ae-0f2a03f6ff27","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfmctBfEwpLVeSg1rHQPq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"We already have most of this. `scripts/telemetry_pull.py`, built 9/29, does all the downloads for you. The useful work now is making it something your colleague can run, and having it catch the hidden-column problem.\n\n**What exists now**\n- It runs the leaderboard in Chrome through Playwright and makes the same clicks a person would: scope, season, group, then More options > Download CSV. It keeps the CSV the page builds byte for byte, so nothing goes through Excel.\n- Two commands pull a full week, 44 files: `--scope FBS`, then `--scope \"FCS,Group of Six\"`. You log in once (`--login`). After that you only keep the window visible.\n- It checks each file as it lands: right tab, right position group, rows > 0, not a repeat of the last file. It also writes a manifest.\n- It stays inside the project rules: clicks only, no auth token, no internal API.\n\n**What I'd change (recommended)**\n1. **Fail on missing columns.** The pull checks the tab but not the full column list, and the loader doesn't either. That's why today's export got as far as it did. I'd compare each file's headers against the matching 2025 file and stop on any missing column (`Elig.`, Tackle Breaking, and so on). I'd add the same check to the LOAD STATUS tab, so a hand-downloaded file with hidden columns says \"MISSING COLUMNS\" instead of loading quietly.\n2. **One-click weekly pull.** A `pull_week.bat` would run both scopes into a dated folder (`_exports/2026_wk06/`) and print the manifest summary. Then it's pull, paste the folder path into UPDATE DATA, Refresh All. The 44 downloads take no clicks.\n3. **Set up your colleague's machine once.** He needs `uv` and a one-time `--login` with his own Telemetry account. I haven't checked whether column visibility is saved on his account or only in his browser. If it's on his account, the pull would export with his hidden columns too, so check 1 matters either way.\n\n**What won't make it faster**\n- **Fewer files.** The leaderboard only shows metrics after you pick a position group, and each group has different columns. So it's 11 groups × 2 tabs per scope.\n- **Calling Telemetry's API directly.** It would be much faster, but reading the token or calling internal services is blocked by project rule 3.\n- **Pulling only the Transfer Portal scope.** It's a smaller file but still 22 downloads, and it would lose the pre-portal board.\n\nTime: I didn't record how long a full 22-file run takes. A rough guess is a few minutes per scope, and nobody has to click anything during it.\n\nShould I build 1 and 2? It's a small change to `telemetry_pull.py` plus the .bat, and no new numbered workbook. The LOAD STATUS check would go into 019, since 018 stays as shipped."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1242,"cache_read_input_tokens":114597,"output_tokens":1441,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":493},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1242,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1441,"cache_read_input_tokens":114597,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1242,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1242},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfmctBQMXWmU5MEtVKuoa","type":"assistant","uuid":"47806d5b-7ba2-409a-84a3-9e9410376466","timestamp":"2026-10-06T20:32:22.759Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"d1673601-88f7-4fb0-b