{"parentUuid":"7d407cea-9424-4242-a1be-8aad0ca8f039","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"b9492239-3e1e-4c1a-81f1-01c3172a67db","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VarjjGf8o4E9QMDccyuYcb","type":"tool_result","content":"Already up to date.\nLoadStatus.m\nPortalInput.m\nStage.m\n# STATUS\n\nRead this first. Update it before ending every session.\n\n## Current state\n\n- **2026 FBS leaderboard pulled (2026-09-29, through week 5): 22 CSVs in Drive\n  `_exports/2026_asof_2026-09-29/fbs/` + `manifest_2026_fbs.json`.** 138 teams\n  (RB traits 137), headers and BOM match the 2025 files, all 22 distinct.\n  `scripts/telemetry_pull.py` now works end to end: scope fix `20e2de6`; `93e8829`\n  keeps the CSV the page builds for Download CSV instead of Chrome's download\n  manager, which crashed Chrome seconds after each download (Crashpad dumps in\n  the tool profile), and lets the manifest merge across reruns. Not yet loaded\n  into a workbook. Handoffs: `docs/handoffs/2026-09-29-telemetry-pull-fix.md`,\n  `docs/handoffs/2026-09-29-2026-fbs-pull.md`.\n- **018 (2026-09-30) is the current staff workbook, in Send/.** 017 with the\n  DeJean provenance fix: `RETURN_ROLE` keyed to one raw row (season, source,\n  player, heading, selectors), DeJean's 2023 SI kick-returner row excluded, his\n  DB All-America kept; the matcher stops if an entry does not match exactly one\n  row. Benchmark CSV identical to v4; versus 017 only HONORS BENCHMARK A3 differs\n  (note rewritten); `check_workbook.py` ALL CHECKS PASS. v4 outputs in\n  `_exports/honors/superseded_2026-09-30_v4/`. 017 also stays in Send/ because it\n  went to Mauro today; every number is the same. Sonnet 5.5 review of 018 (Codex at usage limit): SHIP, all 6 checks pass (`docs/audits/2026-09-30-sonnet-check-018.md`); its per-entry guard suggestion applied, outputs identical.\n- **017 (2026-09-30), superseded by 018; sent to Mauro.** 016 with one All-American flag removed: Codex's check of\n  016 (`docs/audits/2026-09-30-codex-check-016.md`) passed everything except\n  LaJohntay Wester 2023, whose All-America award was as punt returner (FWAA,\n  Phil Steele). `honors_match.py` `RETURN_ROLE` now lists sourced returner\n  exceptions. 15 WR All-American medians moved, as Codex predicted; 40 cells\n  differ from 016; `check_workbook.py` passes on 017. v3 outputs and a raw\n  snapshot in `_exports/honors/superseded_2026-09-30_v3/`.\nShell cwd was reset to G:\\My Drive\\00_Primary_Storage_Drive\\02_SPORTS\\Football\\PP_Recruiting","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"2daab256-74be-4974-b6a5-725df63b0d76","timestamp":"2026-10-06T20:41:17.505Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"Already up to date.\nLoadStatus.m\nPortalInput.m\nStage.m\n# STATUS\n\nRead this first. Update it before ending every session.\n\n## Current state\n\n- **2026 FBS leaderboard pulled (2026-09-29, through week 5): 22 CSVs in Drive\n  `_exports/2026_asof_2026-09-29/fbs/` + `manifest_2026_fbs.json`.** 138 teams\n  (RB traits 137), headers and BOM match the 2025 files, all 22 distinct.\n  `scripts/telemetry_pull.py` now works end to end: scope fix `20e2de6`; `93e8829`\n  keeps the CSV the page builds for Download CSV instead of Chrome's download\n  manager, which crashed Chrome seconds after each download (Crashpad dumps in\n  the tool profile), and lets the manifest merge across reruns. Not yet loaded\n  into a workbook. Handoffs: `docs/handoffs/2026-09-29-telemetry-pull-fix.md`,\n  `docs/handoffs/2026-09-29-2026-fbs-pull.md`.\n- **018 (2026-09-30) is the current staff workbook, in Send/.** 017 with the\n  DeJean provenance fix: `RETURN_ROLE` keyed to one raw row (season, source,\n  player, heading, selectors), DeJean's 2023 SI kick-returner row excluded, his\n  DB All-America kept; the matcher stops if an entry does not match exactly one\n  row. Benchmark CSV identical to v4; versus 017 only HONORS BENCHMARK A3 differs\n  (note rewritten); `check_workbook.py` ALL CHECKS PASS. v4 outputs in\n  `_exports/honors/superseded_2026-09-30_v4/`. 017 also stays in Send/ because it\n  went to Mauro today; every number is the same. Sonnet 5.5 review of 018 (Codex at usage limit): SHIP, all 6 checks pass (`docs/audits/2026-09-30-sonnet-check-018.md`); its per-entry guard suggestion applied, outputs identical.\n- **017 (2026-09-30), superseded by 018; sent to Mauro.** 016 with one All-American flag removed: Codex's check of\n  016 (`docs/audits/2026-09-30-codex-check-016.md`) passed everything except\n  LaJohntay Wester 2023, whose All-America award was as punt returner (FWAA,\n  Phil Steele). `honors_match.py` `RETURN_ROLE` now lists sourced returner\n  exceptions. 15 WR All-American medians moved, as Codex predicted; 40 cells\n  differ from 016; `check_workbook.py` passes on 017. v3 outputs and a raw\n  snapshot in `_exports/honors/superseded_2026-09-30_v3/`.","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to G:\\My Drive\\00_Primary_Storage_Drive\\02_SPORTS\\Football\\PP_Recruiting","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"7d407cea-9424-4242-a1be-8aad0ca8f039","session_id":"d1673601-88f7-4fb0-b59a-00f5414c1656","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"G:\\My Drive\\00_Primary_Storage_Drive\\02_SPORTS\\Football\\PP_Recruiting","sessionId":"d1673601-88f7-4fb0-b59a-00f5414c1656","version":"2.1.291","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
