6 load: 44 leaderboard CSVs (FBS + FCS/G6\n   in one folder; season 2026, all 11 groups, Player Traits + Advanced Stats),\n   Min Elig 1. Check LOAD STATUS: unmapped columns none, unknown codes only ST.\n   Tell him a refresh takes 2-4 minutes. Week-5 REVIEW + Sample OK by tab (item 0\n   load): QB 68, RB 48, WR/SLOT 168, TE 54, OT 175, OG 316, NT 88, END/JACK 122,\n   ILB/JACK 141, CB/STAR 156, SAF/STAR 149. All clear his 30; only RB sits in\n   30-50. **OG/OT: show as is (Eric, 2026-09-30).** No trim for the walkthrough;\n   tell Mauro the Profile BOTH path (200+ snaps, OT/OG/C/EDGE) inflates them.\n   Trimming stays an open question (same as OL targets vs honoree medians).\n   **Send 017 as is (Eric, 2026-09-30)** with the email in\n   `docs/2026-09-30-mauro-email-017.md`; the Codex DeJean finding changes no number.\n- Size versus Player Impact for proven undersized players; band sort versus a\n  rank, given the no-composite rule.\n\n## Gotchas\n\n- `telemetry_pull.py` uses one Chrome profile (`%LOCALAPPDATA%\\telemetry-pull`);\n  only one run at a time. Two sessions pulling at once lock each other out\n  (\"Opening in existing browser session\"), and a hung diagnostic holds the lock.\n  Chrome's download manager crashes this machine's automated Chrome a few\n  seconds after a download; the tool no longer uses it (page CSV captured\n  instead). Do not revert to `expect_download`/`save_as`.\n46:        # their first refresh, so both tables get their first refresh before any\n47:        # layout is written; the folder is read from a temporary cell meanwhile.\n2026_fcs-g6_CB_advanced-stats.csv\n2026_fcs-g6_CB_player-traits.csv\n2026_fcs-g6_EDGE_advanced-stats.csv\nShell cwd was reset to G:\\My Drive\\00_Primary_Storage_Drive\\02_SPORTS\\Football\\PP_Recruiting","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"48ca9c62-20c9-408d-9b9f-5195407cdd72","timestamp":"2026-10-06T20:41:37.825Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"- Review trigger: elite-trait share at or above 0.375\n- Minimum graded trai