{"parentUuid":"44b8e2a5-1148-480d-88d5-b3b481f27124","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"b9492239-3e1e-4c1a-81f1-01c3172a67db","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011cHDvPWebMMCHJwsix9sup","type":"tool_result","content":"The file C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\Desktop\\DEV\\PP_Recruiting\\scripts\\pull_week.bat has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"87953df5-b515-4bdd-bcf4-780a0f5814b8","timestamp":"2026-10-06T20:55:16.140Z","toolUseResult":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\Desktop\\DEV\\PP_Recruiting\\scripts\\pull_week.bat","oldString":"set \"EXPORTS=G:\\My Drive\\00_Primary_Storage_Drive\\02_SPORTS\\Football\\PP_Recruiting\\_exports\"\n","newString":"set \"EXPORTS=G:\\My Drive\\00_Primary_Storage_Drive\\02_SPORTS\\Football\\PP_Recruiting\\_exports\"\nif defined PP_EXPORTS set \"EXPORTS=%PP_EXPORTS%\"\n","originalFile":"@echo off\nrem pull_week: the weekly Telemetry pull in one step.\nrem   Downloads all 44 leaderboard CSVs (FBS, then FCS + Group of Six; 11 groups x\nrem   Player Traits + Advanced Stats) into ONE dated folder on Drive, checks every\nrem   file (check_exports.py), and copies the folder path to the clipboard for the\nrem   UPDATE DATA tab.\nrem\nrem   scripts\\pull_week.bat            pull the current season\nrem   scripts\\pull_week.bat 2026       pull a given season\nrem   scripts\\pull_week.bat login      log in to Telemetry once (you type the password)\nrem\nrem   Keep the Chrome window it opens visible until it finishes. Run it again the\nrem   same day to retry anything that failed: files already pulled are skipped.\nsetlocal\nset \"REPO=%~dp0..\"\nset \"EXPORTS=G:\\My Drive\\00_Primary_Storage_Drive\\02_SPORTS\\Football\\PP_Recruiting\\_exports\"\nset \"UV=%USERPROFILE%\\.local\\bin\\uv.exe\"\nif not exist \"%UV%\" set \"UV=uv\"\nset \"PULL=\"%UV%\" run --no-project --with playwright python \"%REPO%\\scripts\\telemetry_pull.py\"\"\n\nif /i \"%~1\"==\"login\" (\n  %PULL% --login\n  goto :eof\n)\n\nfor /f %%d in ('powershell -NoProfile -Command \"Get-Date -Format yyyy-MM-dd\"') do set \"TODAY=%%d\"\nset \"SEASON=%~1\"\nif \"%SEASON%\"==\"\" set \"SEASON=%TODAY:~0,4%\"\nset \"OUT=%EXPORTS%\\%SEASON%_asof_%TODAY%\"\necho Pulling season %SEASON% into \"%OUT%\"\necho.\n\necho === FBS ===\n%PULL% --season %SEASON% --scope FBS --out \"%OUT%\"\nset \"FBS_RC=%ERRORLEVEL%\"\necho.\necho === FCS + Group of Six ===\n%PULL% --season %SEASON% --scope \"FCS,Group of Six\" --tag fcs-g6 --out \"%OUT%\"\nset \"FCS_RC=%ERRORLEVEL%\"\necho.\n\necho === Checking the files ===\n\"%UV%\" run --no-project python \"%REPO%\\scripts\\check_exports.py\" \"%OUT%\"\nset \"CHECK_RC=%ERRORLEVEL%\"\necho.\n\nif not \"%FBS_RC%%FCS_RC%%CHECK_RC%\"==\"000\" (\n  echo NOT READY. Some files failed or have problems ^(see above^).\n  echo Run scripts\\pull_week.bat %SEASON% again to retry; files already pulled are skipped.\n  exit /b 1\n)\n<nul set /p \"=%OUT%\" | clip\necho READY. 44 files in:\necho   %OUT%\necho That path is on the clipboard. In the workbook: UPDATE DATA, paste it into the\necho yellow folder cell, then Data ^> Refresh All ^(2-4 minutes^).\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":14,"oldLines":6,"newStart":14,"newLines":7,"lines":[" setlocal"," set \"REPO=%~dp0..\""," set \"EXPORTS=G:\\My Drive\\00_Primary_Storage_Drive\\02_SPORTS\\Football\\PP_Recruiting\\_exports\"","+if defined PP_EXPORTS set \"EXPORTS=%PP_EXPORTS%\""," set \"UV=%USERPROFILE%\\.local\\bin\\uv.exe\""," if not exist \"%UV%\" set \"UV=uv\""," set \"PULL=\"%UV%\" run --no-project --with playwright python \"%REPO%\\scripts\\telemetry_pull.py\"\""]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"44b8e2a5-1148-480d-88d5-b3b481f27124","session_id":"d1673601-88f7-4fb0-b59a-00f5414c1656","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"G:\\My Drive\\00_Primary_Storage_Drive\\02_SPORTS\\Football\\PP_Recruiting","sessionId":"d1673601-88f7-4fb0-b59a-00f5414c1656","version":"2.1.291","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
